- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: The source text consistently attributes all steps to "the customer", but the model assigns every node to a generic "Default" actor, misrepresenting participant responsibilities. (SMC7)
- `action(n1, "start process")` and `action(n11, "end process")`: These actions are not mentioned in the source description and constitute hallucinated behaviors. (SMC1)
- `precedence(n4, n5)`: The source states "Once the invoice is received, the customer should review the pricing...", yet the model jumps directly from `action(n4, "wait for invoice")` to `action(n5, "review pricing and terms")`, omitting the documented invoice receipt step. (SMC1)